  "review": {
    "book": "JDG",
    "entityID": "person:jephthah_839",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "JDG11:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now Jephthah the Gileadite was a mighty man of valor. He was the son of a prostitute. Gilead became the father of Jephthah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG11:2",
        "textualBasisJa": "Gilead’s wife bore him sons. When his wife’s sons grew up, they drove Jephthah out and said to him, “You will not inherit in our father’s house, for you are the son of another woman.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG11:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Jephthah fled from his brothers and lived in the land of Tob. Outlaws joined up with Jephthah, and they went out with him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG11:5",
        "textualBasisJa": "When the children of Ammon made war against Israel, the elders of Gilead went to get Jephthah out of the land of Tob."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG11:6",
        "textualBasisJa": "They said to Jephthah, “Come and be our chief, that we may fight with the children of Ammon.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG11:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "Jephthah said to the elders of Gilead, “Didn’t you hate me, and drive me out of my father’s house? Why have you come to me now when you are in distress?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG11:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "The elders of Gilead said to Jephthah, “Therefore we have turned again to you now, that you may go with us and fight with the children of Ammon. You will be our head over all the inhabitants of Gilead.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG11:9",
        "textualBasisJa": "Jephthah said to the elders of Gilead, “If you bring me home again to fight with the children of Ammon, and the LORD delivers them before me, will I be your head?”"
      },
      {
